  "negative_referents": [],
  "notes": "identify_workspace's selector returns two team_id tuples (T01WORKSPACE via #engineering/#core-infra/U01AGENBOT9, and T02NOVA via #nova-eng/#nova-infra/U_NOVA_OPS), matching the design's underspecified two-alternative resolution; the solver/task must pick or flag both. The wrong-emoji, wrong-message, and non-infra-member negatives are each embedded inside a team that already legitimately qualifies via its own correct chain, so no third, spuriously-selected workspace is produced by these negatives — hence negative_referents is empty at the team (root-entity) level; the negatives instead test that the selector's per-filter conjunction (message content + reaction_type=eyes + channel_members join to the infra channel) rejects those specific rows rather than admitting a bogus extra tuple. U01AGENBOT9 was granted channel_members rows in C_NOVA_ENG/C_NOVA_INFRA and a user_teams row in T02NOVA so conversations.history/replies/members can be used to discover and verify the T02 chain and so conversations.create can plausibly target team_id=T02NOVA if that alternative is chosen. The create_channel selector checks for absence of any pre-existing 'retro-notes' channel."
}
